ext":"Radiant","is_correct":true},{"id":"d","text":"Ascendant","is_correct":false}],"explanation":"The ladder ends at Radiant, above Immortal; only the top players of each region hold it."},{"id":"q7","question":"What role do self-sufficient entry agents like Jett and Reyna play?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Initiator","is_correct":false},{"id":"b","text":"Controller","is_correct":false},{"id":"c","text":"Sentinel","is_correct":false},{"id":"d","text":"Duelist","is_correct":true}],"explanation":"Duelists carry kits built for taking the first fight — dashes, flashes and self-healing."},{"id":"q8","question":"In a standard competitive match, how many rounds does a team need to win?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"10","is_correct":false},{"id":"b","text":"12","is_correct":false},{"id":"c","text":"13","is_correct":true},{"id":"d","text":"16","is_correct":false}],"explanation":"First to 13 wins; at 12–12 the match goes to overtime."}]'::jsonb,
